<title>USA: Warner-Lambert's Lipitor cleared in Canada.</title>
<headline>Warner-Lambert's Lipitor cleared in Canada.</headline>
<dateline>MORRIS PLAINS, N.J. 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warner-Lambert Co said Monday it received  marketing clearance in Canada for Lipitor, a lipid-lowering agent.</p>
<p>The approval in Canada follows a similar approval in the United States, Germany and Britain. Lipitor became available to patients in the United States in February 1997.</p>
<p>Lipitor, an HMG-CoA reductase inhibitor or &quot;statin,&quot; is used for reduction of total cholesterol, LDL- cholesterol, apolipoprotein B, and triglycerides in patients with hypercholesterolemia and mixed dyslipidemia.</p>
